# Bitbucket CODEOWNERS Template
#
# Location in consuming repository: .bitbucket/CODEOWNERS
# Reference: https://support.atlassian.com/bitbucket-cloud/docs/set-up-and-use-code-owners/
#
# ─── SYNTAX OVERVIEW ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Pattern matching follows .gitignore rules with the following exceptions
# (these do NOT work in CODEOWNERS):
#   - Escaping # with \ (# always starts a comment)
#   - Negation with !
#   - Character ranges with [ ]
#
# Precedence: the LAST matching pattern wins.
# More specific rules should therefore appear LOWER in this file.
#
# ─── USER REFERENCE FORMATS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   individual@example.com          Plain email address
#   @username                       Bitbucket username (@ prefix)
#   @workspace-slug/group-slug      Workspace group (workspace slug / group slug)
#   @teams/team-name                Ad-hoc team defined in teams.yaml
#
# ─── SELECTION STRATEGIES ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   (default / omitted)             One random user from the group
#   :random                         Same as :random(1)
#   :random(N)                      N random users from the group
#   :least_busy                     Same as :least_busy(1) — fewest open reviews
#   :least_busy(N)                  N least-busy users from the group
#   :all                            Every member of the group
#
#   Inline strategies override the strategy defined in teams.yaml.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Global fallback owner ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Matches every file not covered by a more specific rule below.
# Replace with the team/individual responsible for overall repository health.
#
* {{global-owner@example.com}}

# ── Source code — by technology ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Assign technology-specific teams so reviewers have domain expertise.
# Adjust extensions and owner references to match your stack.
#
*.py        @teams/backend
*.java      @teams/backend
*.ts        @teams/frontend
*.tsx       @teams/frontend
*.js        @teams/frontend
*.sql       @teams/dba:least_busy(2)

# ── Application modules ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# More specific path rules take precedence over the extension rules above
# because they appear lower in the file.
#
/src/frontend/*     @teams/frontend
/src/backend/*      @teams/backend
/src/database/*     @teams/dba

# ── Critical / high-risk paths ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Require all senior reviewers for security-sensitive or high-impact paths.
#
/src/security/*         @teams/seniors:all
/src/auth/*             @teams/seniors:all
/src/keys/*.pub         @teams/sre {{superuser@example.com}}

# ── Infrastructure and CI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/infra/*            @teams/sre
/.github/*          @teams/sre
/.bitbucket/*       {{devops-lead@example.com}}  # meta-owner for VCS config

# ── Documentation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/docs/*             {{tech-writer@example.com}}
*.md                {{tech-writer@example.com}}

# ── Doctrine / agent framework ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Restrict changes to the agent governance framework to designated owners.
/doctrine/*         {{framework-owner@example.com}}
/.doctrine-config/* {{framework-owner@example.com}}
/AGENTS.md          {{framework-owner@example.com}}
